; BALANCES row order (#2409) with renamed roots: account_sortkey classifies
; against the `name_*` options, so Debts (liabilities) sorts before Capital
; (equity), and Revenue (income) before Spending (expenses), although plain
; name order puts Capital first. Assets keeps its name so the corpus query
; `BALANCES FROM has_account('Assets')` matches.

option "name_liabilities" "Debts"
option "name_equity" "Capital"
option "name_income" "Revenue"
option "name_expenses" "Spending"

2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank USD
2024-01-01 open Debts:Card USD
2024-01-01 open Capital:Opening USD
2024-01-01 open Revenue:Job USD
2024-01-01 open Spending:Food USD

2024-01-02 * "Opening balance"
  Assets:Bank      500.00 USD
  Capital:Opening

2024-01-15 * "Pay"
  Assets:Bank     2000.00 USD
  Revenue:Job

2024-02-03 * "Groceries"
  Spending:Food     40.00 USD
  Assets:Bank

2024-02-05 * "Card payment"
  Debts:Card        25.00 USD
  Assets:Bank
